Candidate: Preserve taint and identity through native JavaScript Array.fill
Base-Commit: 71255b1345d44e89a1f7208e58579b4c2ced5d0f
Status: HISTORICAL CANDIDATE; superseded by the active main implementation.

Commit 781ec7b5acd854f5ce4ab6e342deb1ab15a177fd activated the bounded fill
implementation with an additional comma-expression correction in 5.5.63.
Subsequent native probes exposed descriptor/getter side effects that this
original candidate does not guard. Use the current helper and regression
tests; do not reapply this historical patch. Its original diff and hashes
remain unchanged below. The following notes describe its archival state.

The executor disconnected before the paired DSR run returned a usable result.
This implementation and its regression tests are retained for runtime
qualification; they are not loaded by UBS. Existing expectations and gates
are unchanged. Independent static review and native JavaScript examples check
the intended semantics and fixture labels, not the analyzer implementation.

Scope: native Array.fill on modeled array allocations; alias/return identity;
literal bounds with negative offsets, fractions, null/undefined, NaN/infinities;
holes, clean overwrites, sanitizer domains and finite work-budget accounting.
Unknown ranges use conservative writes. Opaque bound conversions, explicit
descriptors, restriction APIs and prior unknown escapes cannot certify a clean
fill: the existing incomplete-analysis channel carries those boundaries.
Relevant Object APIs retain returned array identity and prior descriptor or
prototype provenance; modeled Reflect methods return Boolean facts.
Property-contract metadata stays on heap identity and is excluded from copies.
Generic borrowed fill, arbitrary setters/coercion, exact BigInt completion and
other unmodeled JavaScript protocols remain outside this bounded slice.

Before activation: reconcile with current main, run all new and existing
JavaScript taint/security tests plus real CLI JSON/SARIF checks, refresh the
canonical checksums/version as required by AGENTS.md, and run the prescribed
quality gates through DSR. Do not treat this archive or native fixture checks
as runtime qualification or close the parent D6 production-completeness work.

